#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.10"
# dependencies = ["anthropic>=2.3,<3"]
# ///
"""approve-all: keep Claude Code sessions moving by taking their recommendation.

Runs as a Claude Code hook. When a session stops to ask something, it replies
with the option the session recommended and the session carries on:

  Stop               wrap-up buttons take the first one (the session's pick);
                     other questions get "go with your recommendation";
                     "paste this into the other session" gets told to send it itself
  AskUserQuestion    picks the "(Recommended)" option, else the first
  PermissionRequest  allows

Some things are never answered for you. See NEVER below. A dialog asks you instead,
with answers to pick from, and sends your pick straight to the session. It stays up
for APPROVE_ALL_ANSWER_WAIT seconds and closes early if the session gets a message
another way. The same happens when a session repeats a question or goes
APPROVE_ALL_MAX_IDLE turns without doing any work.

With an API key, Claude reviews each decision first using the session's recent
activity: whether anything is really being asked, which option fits, and what only
you can do. It can't lift NEVER. If a review fails or the budget runs out, the rules
above take over. Change it with APPROVE_ALL_MODEL, APPROVE_ALL_EFFORT and
APPROVE_ALL_BUDGET_USD.

The key and settings go in a .env next to this script; see .env.example. Run this
through uv, which brings the SDK: uv run --script approve-all status

  approve-all set-key               save the API key outside .env (or: pbpaste | approve-all set-key)
  approve-all check                 make one real review call to test the key
  approve-all install | uninstall   add or remove the hooks in ~/.claude/settings.json
  approve-all pause | resume        stop or restart answering, in every session, at once
  approve-all scan [--hours 24]     list sessions waiting right now (read-only)
  approve-all log [-n 20]           show recent decisions
  approve-all status
"""
